\",\n  \"teacher_diagnosis\": \"The 1.7B quantized model (Qwen3-1.7B-Q4_K_M) cannot perform the required filesystem enumeration and content analysis. It hallucinated a plausible but incorrect summary (5 files, 3 families, prefixes 'capability_loop'/'reviewed'/'test') instead of the true corpus (24 files, 8 families, prefixes blocked/frontdoor/logic/prompt/queue). The model appears to have inferred filenames from the directory path components rather than actually listing the directory. Both attempts produced identical output, confirming deterministic failure at this capability level. The prompt is well-formed and unambiguous; the failure is purely a model-capability gap.\",\n  \"candidate_prompt_patch\": null,\n  \"retry_guidance\": \"No prompt modification will resolve this. The task requires actual filesystem access (directory listing, file reading, field extraction) which the model cannot perform in a single inference call without tool use. Options: (1) Pre-compute the answer and embed it as a few-shot example in the prompt, reducing the task to pattern-matching; (2) Use a tool-augmented agent that can actually list files and read contents; (3) Use a larger model with stronger instruction-following and arithmetic; (4) Decompose into sub-tasks where the harness provides the raw file list and the model only performs counting/grouping.\",\n  \"corrected_reference_output\": {\n    \"cover_all_files\": false,\n    \"distinct_task_families\": 8,\n    \"filename_prefix_groups\": {\n      \"blocked\": 4,\n      \"frontdoor\": 5,\n      \"logic\": 6,\n      \"prompt\": 6,\n      \"queue\": 3\n    },\n    \"readme_named_source_families\": 4,\n    \"total_files\": 24\n  }\n}\n```", "metadata": {"configured_model": "Qwen3.8-27B-UD-IQ4_XS.gguf", "endpoint_alias": "JARVIS_LOCAL", "error": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "model": "Qwen3.8-27B-UD-IQ4_XS.gguf", "model_resolution_attempted": false, "model_resolution_error": null, "request_provenance": {"api": "openai-chat", "append_